   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend part E of a chapter of the laws of 2017, amending the vehicle and traffic law relating to reciprocal agreements concerning suspension or revocation of registration of a motor vehicle for violations of toll collection regulations, as proposed in legislative bill numbers S. 2008-C and A. 3008-C, in relation to reporting requirements",
    "basePrintNo": "S6008",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6008-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Part E §2, Chap of 2017 (as proposed in S.2008-C and A.3008-C)",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6008\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend part E of a chapter of the laws of\n2017, amending the vehicle and traffic law relating to reciprocal\nagreements concerning suspension or revocation of registration of a\nmotor vehicle for violations of toll collection regulations, as\nproposed in legislative bill numbers S. 2008-C and A. 3008-C, in\nrelation to reporting requirements\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nTo amend provisions of a Chapter of the Laws of 2017 relating to the\nreporting of reciprocal agreements by the Commissioner of Motor\nVehicles.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nThe bill amends a Chapter of the Laws of 2017 to require that the\nreport by the Commissioner of Motor Vehicles of all reciprocal\nagreements entered into by each tolling authority be submitted on or\nbefore the first day of February of each year.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe 2017-2018 Budget authorized each tolling authority in the state to\nenter into reciprocal agreements with other states in order to collect\nfrom out-of-state toll violators. It also requires the Commissioner of\nMotor Vehicles, in consultation with the tolling authorities, to\nsubmit a report to the governor and legislature that, in part,\nidentifies each reciprocal agreement entered into pursuant to this\nsection. By making submission of this report an annual requirement,\nthis transparency would be continued in subsequent years.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nUnknown.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as\na Chapter of the Laws of 2017, amending the vehicle and traffic law\nrelating to reciprocal agreements concerning suspension or revocation\nof registration of a motor vehicle for violations of toll collection\nregulations.\n",
